WEBVTT

00:06:01.065 --> 00:06:03.484
And we’re coupling
this on-the-ground monitoring

00:06:03.484 --> 00:06:05.694
with high-resolution
satellite observations

00:06:05.694 --> 00:06:07.947
and advanced computer modeling

00:06:07.947 --> 00:06:11.492
so that we can track
the changing Arctic in near real-time

00:06:11.492 --> 00:06:14.870
and accurately project
permafrost emissions into the future.

00:06:16.455 --> 00:06:19.208
But state-of-the-art science
just isn’t enough.

00:06:20.209 --> 00:06:23.337
We need to make sure
that permafrost emissions are counted

00:06:23.337 --> 00:06:25.297
when setting global emissions targets,

00:06:25.297 --> 00:06:29.468
because each year that we fail
to account for permafrost is another year

00:06:29.468 --> 00:06:33.013
that we become unwittingly locked-in
to more severe climate warming.